# 6.1's text normaliser, lifted the same way, with the six rules it calls
# that 4.3 never had. It reads a word typed against digits or a bracket as
# a word, and a path, a web address or an email address as one.

rule normalize_text takes 3
  instead
  local c100 bytes 8
  local c120 bytes 8
  local c130 bytes 8
